{"operation": "CGS-RUN", "event": "commit_start", "message": "cgitsync3.9.0 A tree is now a user's or a developer's by what it holds: status prints profile=user or profile=dev, and status --json carries it. A developer's tree whose .cgs declares no memory is offered one, in a terminal and only once: the new memory setup command creates the repository, adds it to the .cgs and adopts the local memory. Everywhere else, memory status included, it warns that the work has no memory back-up, and names the command that fixes it.", "stage_all": true, "scope": "writable"}
